Acknowledgement timing as quic-go decides it (hysteria client).

quic-go, in the application data space (vendor/quic-go/internal/ackhandler/
received_packet_tracker.go:78-228, packet_packer.go:724-730):
  - the delayed-ACK alarm is a flat MaxAckDelay, 25 ms, whatever the RTT;
  - an ACK is queued at once only when the packet was reported missing by the last ACK sent, when
    two ack-eliciting packets have arrived since it, when a packet is missing at or above that
    ACK's largest acknowledged (reorderingThreshold 1), or on ECN-CE;
  - a pending ACK rides in every packet that carries stream or control data, timer or not.

Upstream ngtcp2 uses min(max_ack_delay, smoothed_rtt/8) for the timer, answers every out-of-order
packet and every new gap at once, and puts an ACK into a data packet only when its timer has run
out or an immediate ACK is due.

This patch: conn_compute_ack_delay returns NGTCP2_DEFAULT_MAX_ACK_DELAY; ngtcp2_acktr records
the largest packet number of the last ACK sent, and pktns_commit_recv_pkt_num applies quic-go's
two reordering rules against it; conn_write_pkt asks for the ACK with no delay when the packet will
carry data. ngtcp2_conn_set_app_stream_data_pending lets the application say that stream data is
coming in a later call for the same packet, since the first call may be a DATAGRAM.
Applies on top of 0002.

